What is Infrastructure Drift?
Infrastructure Drift occurs when someone changes an AWS resource outside Terraform, causing the actual infrastructure to become different from the configuration Terraform manages.
Real-world example
Suppose Terraform creates an EC2 instance with these tags:
Name      = Terraform-State-Demo
ManagedBy = Terraform

Now imagine an administrator opens the AWS Console and manually adds another tag:
Department = DevOps

Terraform configuration does not contain this additional tag.

Now there is a difference between:
- Desired state: Defined in main.tf.
- Actual state: Existing configuration in AWS.
This difference is called Infrastructure Drift.
