3. Our practical objective
We will:
1. Identify our existing EC2 instance.
2. Manually modify its tags using AWS CLI.
3. Run Terraform plan.
4. Observe how Terraform detects the difference.
5. Understand how Terraform can reconcile the infrastructure.
Important: We will not change the instance type or terminate the EC2 instance. This exercise only changes a tag.

Step 1: Identify the EC2 instance
Make sure you are inside Practical 4:

aws ec2 describe-instances \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --filters "Name=tag:Name,Values=Terraform-State-Demo" \
  --query "Reservations[*].Instances[*].[InstanceId,State.Name]" \
  --output table

---------------------------------------
|          DescribeInstances          |
+----------------------+--------------+
|  i-0085087d8a4cea024 |  terminated  |
|  i-007355bbe76c8427f |  running     |
+----------------------+--------------+
Step 2: Add a tag manually
Copy the instance ID from the previous output.

Verify:

echo "$INSTANCE_ID"
Add the manual tag
aws ec2 create-tags \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --resources "$INSTANCE_ID" \
  --tags Key=Department,Value=DevOps

Verify the tag

aws ec2 describe-tags \
  --region ap-south-1 \
  --filters "Name=resource-id,Values=$INSTANCE_ID" \
  --output table

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|                                 DescribeTags                                  |
